ambo who was the  second person to take on the mantle  it's the media who originally dubs  monica captain marvel  astonished by her energy-based abilities  but curiously  her take on the name has nothing to do  with marvel or the cree  make sense perfectly not confusing  you can draw a straight line from carol  danvers's powers to the original marvel  but monica's powers and origin story  come from a completely different source  meaning that in marvel comics canon the  fact that they shared a name is  actually just a giant confusing  coincidence although she goes on to  change her hero names several times  throughout the years monica will always  be remembered as the first woman to kick  butt  as captain marvel monica rambo has made  many lasting marks on the history of the  marvel universe  when the avengers made her a  full-fledged member in 1983's avengers  number 231 monica officially became the  first african-american woman to join the  team's ranks  although she was then still pretty new  to the superhero life  both wasp the team's leader at the time  and captain america  her second in command admired monica's  powerful abilities and iron-clad  composure  monica wasn't the first african-american  heroine to join a marvel super team  that honor goes to aurora monroe better  known as the weather manipulating mutant  storm  who made her comic debut in 1975's giant  size  x-men number one in joining the avengers  monica continued a proud history and  blazed a trail into the future  throughout the years  a plethora of marvel superheroes have  led the avengers ranging from popular  characters like luke cage  to lesser known types like dr druid  carol danvers then working as ms marvel  has actually led the team before herself  but as it turns out she isn't the only  captain marvel to earn that particular  distinction  captain america actually nominates  monica rambo  then still known as captain marvel for  the team's leadership role in 1987's  avengers number 279  af